WEBVTT

00:07.007 --> 00:08.299
Hyoga…

00:09.926 --> 00:11.845
Are you serious?

00:15.724 --> 00:20.061
Owari Otome-Ryu Kan-Ryu Spear Style!

00:26.234 --> 00:28.695
Wow! Awesome!

00:28.778 --> 00:30.864
Exactly what I said, Hyoga.

00:30.947 --> 00:33.158
We'll be able to dig up a lot
with your skills.

00:33.241 --> 00:37.120
I feel like I'm badly staining
my Kan-Ryu with this…

00:37.203 --> 00:38.621
Staining?

00:39.247 --> 00:40.832
Isn't it the opposite?

00:40.915 --> 00:42.959
There's beauty in the steady progress

00:43.042 --> 00:46.004
that's made while covered in dirt.

00:47.464 --> 00:50.383
However,
if we want to break through bedrock,

00:50.467 --> 00:53.261
we'll need a drill,
science’s ultimate blade.

00:54.637 --> 00:55.847
Yes…

00:56.723 --> 00:58.641
<i>I left the crafting part to him…</i>

01:00.518 --> 01:01.519
<i>Kaseki!</i>

01:05.982 --> 01:10.361
Check this out!
It's my awesome Spinning Knife.

01:10.445 --> 01:13.073
Are we using it
to stab the enemy in the stomach?

01:13.740 --> 01:15.492
It doesn't look bad.

01:15.575 --> 01:16.618
Going for the entrails?

01:16.701 --> 01:18.870
You two are scary!

01:18.953 --> 01:21.706
I don't know how it's supposed to be used,

01:21.790 --> 01:26.419
but even I was shocked
by how lethal this blade looks.

01:26.503 --> 01:28.922
It's meant for digging in the ground,
isn't it?

01:29.005 --> 01:31.841
We've got to deliver this blade of science

01:31.925 --> 01:34.344
and the lab car to Chrome's site.

01:35.386 --> 01:37.597
All right! Let's get going!

01:38.181 --> 01:40.266
<i>We'll show them what a counterattack</i>

01:40.809 --> 01:43.436
<i>from the Kingdom of Science's</i>
<i>combined forces looks like!</i>

01:45.563 --> 01:50.485
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

03:21.326 --> 03:23.995
A tunnel feels like
an extreme construction project.

03:24.829 --> 03:26.372
Whoever delivers it shouldn't return.

03:26.456 --> 03:29.000
They should just stay
and help with the construction.

03:29.083 --> 03:32.170
But if there are too many of them,
the enemy will likely spot them.

03:34.297 --> 03:38.885
In that case, it's time for the man
with the strength of a hundred to step in.

03:57.111 --> 03:58.863
Luna! Yuzuriha!

03:59.906 --> 04:02.242
I leave Senku to you.

04:19.384 --> 04:21.344
Some kind of car is leaving the ship!

04:21.427 --> 04:23.221
Should one of us go after it?

04:23.888 --> 04:27.558
Good! I'll stay close to my lady.
You go after it!

04:31.312 --> 04:34.065
What's the point
if I, the bodyguard, am not here?

04:34.148 --> 04:35.900
You should go, since you're the driver!

04:35.984 --> 04:38.236
You're right…

04:44.575 --> 04:47.078
Hey!

04:47.161 --> 04:50.248
-He's the one coming towards us!
-He's the one coming towards us!

04:51.791 --> 04:52.625
Hop!

04:54.085 --> 04:55.837
Greetings!

04:55.920 --> 04:58.339
I'm Taiju. Nice to meet you!

04:58.423 --> 05:01.342
You must be the ones
in charge of surveilling us,

05:01.426 --> 05:03.469
just like Kohaku's team…

05:03.553 --> 05:06.139
No, I shouldn't be telling you this.

05:06.931 --> 05:08.891
I don't understand Japanese at all.

05:08.975 --> 05:11.894
But still, I can somehow
tell what he's saying.

05:11.978 --> 05:15.857
Yes, his voice and gestures
are over the top.

05:15.940 --> 05:17.525
You were going to follow this car

05:17.608 --> 05:19.819
to continue your surveillance duties,
right?

05:20.820 --> 05:24.699
Then, why don't you jump in the back seat
and come with us?

05:24.782 --> 05:26.200
Let's go!

05:28.578 --> 05:30.121
-What the heck?
-What the heck?

05:30.204 --> 05:32.040
We're enemies, aren't we?

05:33.166 --> 05:35.293
We're headed that way anyway.

05:45.678 --> 05:49.015
I wonder if Carlos will be fine.

05:59.692 --> 06:01.819
Is Miss Luna safe?

06:02.862 --> 06:05.615
Sorry, I don't understand English at all.

06:05.698 --> 06:10.495
But, you were asking about Luna, right?

06:12.914 --> 06:16.000
She's taking care of my friend
at this moment.

06:18.336 --> 06:21.756
<i>According to Ryusui, Luna is a spy.</i>

06:21.839 --> 06:23.091
<i>But I really don't care.</i>

06:26.552 --> 06:30.098
<i>She agreed to look after him.</i>

06:30.181 --> 06:31.474
<i>For me, that's enough.</i>

06:32.517 --> 06:35.812
You can be sure we won't treat her badly.

06:35.895 --> 06:37.105
Don't worry.

06:39.315 --> 06:42.860
<i>I don't understand</i>
<i>a single word of Japanese, but…</i>

06:43.444 --> 06:45.988
<i>He doesn’t seem like a bad guy.</i>

06:46.572 --> 06:48.366
<i>I can tell, somehow…</i>

06:50.618 --> 06:51.494
Huh?

06:51.994 --> 06:54.539
Did Taiju have a driver's license?

06:55.581 --> 06:59.043
That time he fled from Moz,
he drove illegally, though.

07:04.757 --> 07:07.093
Wait, wait, wait!

07:07.677 --> 07:10.388
What are you doing?

07:10.471 --> 07:13.307
Sorry! I'm still not used to driving.

07:13.391 --> 07:16.936
Thank you for worrying about me!

07:17.019 --> 07:20.022
I'm a tough guy, I'll be fine!

07:22.733 --> 07:26.696
I'm neither tough nor fine…

07:30.074 --> 07:32.743
Thank you… Carlos, am I right?

07:33.327 --> 07:35.746
You're really good at driving!

07:35.830 --> 07:37.623
You really helped me here!

07:37.707 --> 07:40.668
It's because I'm a professional driver.
I'll take this just in case.

07:42.545 --> 07:46.674
<i>Why am I driving an enemy car?</i>

07:48.009 --> 07:49.594
Is it okay to send a lab car?

07:50.219 --> 07:52.972
Won't the enemy's watchdogs track it?

07:53.055 --> 07:55.808
We'll join Ukyo near the goal.

07:55.892 --> 07:59.187
If they came through the bushes
fast enough to keep up with the car,

07:59.270 --> 08:01.522
Ukyo would definitely hear them.

08:01.606 --> 08:04.317
We'd be able to respond accordingly.

08:05.485 --> 08:07.153
Well…

08:07.737 --> 08:10.072
Never mind my hearing,

08:10.156 --> 08:12.241
I was in the car with them the whole time.

08:13.493 --> 08:15.953
But how did things end up like this?

08:17.747 --> 08:20.583
Why did you capture Carlos?

08:20.666 --> 08:23.669
He's a good guy,
he drove all the way here!

08:23.753 --> 08:25.671
If we released him,

08:25.755 --> 08:28.716
he'd instantly rush to Xeno's fortress.

08:28.799 --> 08:31.677
Wouldn't he reveal
the entire tunnel operation?

08:32.345 --> 08:33.679
Is that so?

08:38.017 --> 08:39.602
"Dummel"?

08:41.020 --> 08:42.647
<i>A tunnel!</i>

08:44.398 --> 08:45.858
Wow! A spinning knife!

08:46.442 --> 08:48.236
And an engine, a drone…

08:48.319 --> 08:50.530
What an awesome mountain of gems!

08:50.613 --> 08:53.366
We can make it with all this, Taiju!

08:53.449 --> 08:56.202
Really? I'm glad to know!

09:06.420 --> 09:08.923
<i>They're just a bunch of kids.</i>

09:09.590 --> 09:12.927
<i>They look a bit younger than my lady…</i>

09:14.095 --> 09:15.930
<i>Maybe they're high schoolers?</i>

09:18.057 --> 09:21.269
Why did you break the drone?

09:21.352 --> 09:23.187
I need the propellers.

09:23.271 --> 09:24.480
PROPELLERS

09:24.564 --> 09:27.316
They will send air into the tunnel
during its construction.

09:27.400 --> 09:30.570
We'd die if we ran out of oxygen.

09:31.153 --> 09:32.321
What about the noise?

09:32.947 --> 09:35.074
We should be fine in this area.

09:35.908 --> 09:39.870
Xeno's plant makes much more noise
when it's operating at full power.

09:40.705 --> 09:42.248
That's his weak spot.

10:34.216 --> 10:35.635
This wall is too strong!

10:35.718 --> 10:39.013
Even human strength can't overcome this.

10:39.639 --> 10:42.266
<i>It's impossible. It's absurd…</i>

10:42.892 --> 10:45.853
<i>Just give up already!</i>

11:32.441 --> 11:35.277
We broke through!

11:35.361 --> 11:38.280
Yes!

11:39.240 --> 11:42.076
<i>Are they for real?</i>

11:44.453 --> 11:47.706
We'll keep going
until we reach our objective.

11:48.624 --> 11:52.962
Step by step, covered in dirt!

12:00.177 --> 12:03.681
We've got the ground,
but we must seize the sky as well.

12:03.764 --> 12:08.102
The final showdown involves
air, ground, and water.

12:08.686 --> 12:11.605
We need to finish the aircraft carrier
and the airplane quickly!

12:11.689 --> 12:14.859
But Senku is the only one who knows how.

12:15.484 --> 12:18.946
Castor beans
are needed for the finishing touch.

12:19.655 --> 12:22.867
Crack the shells,
take the molten part out,

12:22.950 --> 12:24.493
and squeeze…

12:24.577 --> 12:26.871
Hey, you need complete rest!

12:28.289 --> 12:30.833
I excuse myself for bothering the patient,

12:30.916 --> 12:32.293
Dr. Luna.

12:33.085 --> 12:34.545
As much as he'd like to stop,

12:35.671 --> 12:37.882
Senku will not give up
on his science leadership.

12:38.841 --> 12:41.594
Neither will he give up on the fight.

12:43.679 --> 12:46.140
In that case,
smooth communication of command

12:46.223 --> 12:48.726
should be the best treatment.

12:53.147 --> 12:56.567
Next, my maintenance…

12:57.318 --> 13:00.029
Where's the stethoscope?

13:00.112 --> 13:03.324
To check the breath sounds of my lungs…

13:17.254 --> 13:18.589
<i>It's him.</i>

13:21.091 --> 13:23.219
<i>Are we really the same age?</i>

13:25.095 --> 13:29.016
<i>In this stone world, all by himself,</i>

13:29.099 --> 13:32.228
<i>he steadily rebuilt</i>
<i>everything from scratch.</i>

13:36.482 --> 13:38.817
<i>I wasn't wrong…</i>

13:39.443 --> 13:42.238
<i>My intuition is quite good.</i>

13:43.614 --> 13:47.243
<i>This sharp-tongued person…</i>

13:47.826 --> 13:49.161
<i>It was him.</i>

13:51.914 --> 13:53.666
<i>Dr. Senku…</i>

13:58.921 --> 14:00.881
<i>He mustn't die, no matter what!</i>

14:01.757 --> 14:04.677
<i>Well, no one should die, actually!</i>

14:04.760 --> 14:06.887
<i>But, he's the only one…</i>

14:11.058 --> 14:14.311
The respiration in his left lung is weak.

14:14.395 --> 14:17.606
The lung might be filling with blood.

14:18.357 --> 14:23.195
Hey, Luna… Stick a needle in
so the blood can come out.

14:25.531 --> 14:27.366
<i>I'm Luna, the cool woman.</i>

14:27.449 --> 14:31.370
<i>I'm Luna, the mighty woman.</i>
<i>The cool woman, the mighty woman…</i>

14:38.460 --> 14:42.089
If the breathing sounds decrease
after draining out the blood,

14:42.172 --> 14:44.675
that means the blood is leaking through

14:44.758 --> 14:46.927
a small wound inside the lung.

14:47.553 --> 14:52.308
In that case, leave the blood in
and stop the bleeding.

14:52.391 --> 14:54.351
It'll be a bloodbath in any case.

14:54.435 --> 14:56.562
Get me somebody with AB blood.

14:57.563 --> 14:59.940
What did you say? AB blood?

15:00.566 --> 15:04.194
There's no way Luna could know that
all of a sudden!

15:04.904 --> 15:05.821
Luna…

15:07.448 --> 15:10.951
I know you're on the enemy's side.

15:11.035 --> 15:13.829
But you're my only option now…

15:19.460 --> 15:22.296
I just have one favor to ask.

15:22.379 --> 15:23.213
Huh…

15:23.839 --> 15:25.132
"Huh"?

15:25.215 --> 15:28.719
I don't need to hear that, I know already…

15:28.802 --> 15:32.181
But if you just said you'd think about it,

15:32.723 --> 15:36.310
I think I'll have the strength
to give my best…

15:39.313 --> 15:42.316
What are your conditions? Our surrender?

15:43.275 --> 15:44.485
If that's the case…

15:48.113 --> 15:52.076
If you recover… will you go out with me?

15:54.578 --> 15:55.579
What?

15:58.707 --> 16:00.960
We want to know
the layout of the fortress' interior.

16:01.043 --> 16:02.878
If we popped our heads out of the tunnel

16:02.962 --> 16:05.047
and found ourselves
right in front of the barracks,

16:05.130 --> 16:07.424
it would be anything but amusing for us.

16:08.801 --> 16:11.720
Carlos! You already know, right?

16:11.804 --> 16:14.932
Could you draw a map of Xeno's fortress?

16:17.518 --> 16:20.187
There's no way I'd do that! We're enemies!

16:21.021 --> 16:21.939
You're right.

16:26.068 --> 16:28.404
<i>35, 11…</i>

16:29.279 --> 16:32.366
I can't recognize this girl's voice.
Who is she?

16:32.950 --> 16:34.076
<i>33…</i>

16:34.159 --> 16:37.413
My lady! It's my lady Luna! How…?

16:37.496 --> 16:41.083
<i>57, 63…</i>

16:44.795 --> 16:45.754
<i>32…</i>

16:46.880 --> 16:48.632
Did something happen?

16:50.009 --> 16:52.761
Why is he bursting into tears?
What's with those emotions?

16:52.845 --> 16:54.138
Is that…?

16:54.722 --> 16:58.308
I finally got myself a boyfriend.
His name is Senku.

16:58.392 --> 17:00.310
What?

17:00.394 --> 17:02.896
What is this? What does it mean?

17:02.980 --> 17:03.814
Yes…

17:03.897 --> 17:05.774
I can mostly imagine what it is,

17:05.858 --> 17:08.569
but it doesn't seem good.

17:20.414 --> 17:22.249
This is a different story now.

17:22.833 --> 17:25.210
Max and I are my lady's allies

17:25.836 --> 17:28.005
all the way to the ends of hell!

17:30.090 --> 17:34.011
This looks good. You're doing a great job.

17:34.094 --> 17:35.971
If we can sneak into the fortress safely,

17:36.055 --> 17:39.892
we'll just need our infiltrator Gen
to show us around.

17:39.975 --> 17:44.521
But we haven't received any news
from Gen inside the fortress.

17:44.605 --> 17:47.441
Is this an Uesugi Code Table?

17:47.524 --> 17:50.319
They sure look like a bunch
of random numbers to the uninitiated.

17:51.278 --> 17:54.948
Talking about that incredibly
untrustworthy, chatterbox guy.

17:55.532 --> 17:57.076
Let's hope he's doing something!

17:57.159 --> 18:01.288
Decide now! Can we trust him or not?

18:07.878 --> 18:12.382
<i>35, 11, 14…</i>

18:13.592 --> 18:14.593
<i>A code…</i>

18:17.054 --> 18:19.473
<i>Simple and practical.</i>

18:19.556 --> 18:23.477
<i>Indecipherable to Xeno,</i>
<i>but understandable for me.</i>

18:24.353 --> 18:26.563
<i>A fitting approach.</i>

18:29.691 --> 18:33.237
<i>Yes, it's the Uesugi cipher.</i>

18:44.665 --> 18:48.627
Could it be that it's finished?

18:56.218 --> 18:59.179
Splendid, Dr. Brody.

18:59.263 --> 19:02.307
It's actually elegant!

19:07.062 --> 19:11.900
The day for the final project execution
will be the day after tomorrow.

19:13.026 --> 19:18.157
<i>It's a huge vehicle.</i>
<i>This looks really bad…</i>

19:19.324 --> 19:21.451
<i>Even Senku and the others</i>

19:21.535 --> 19:24.872
<i>do not know about this secret weapon</i>
<i>in the stone world…</i>

19:29.918 --> 19:34.047
I've started to date Senku.

19:34.882 --> 19:37.759
But, what is dating even about?

19:37.843 --> 19:39.678
She became philosophical.

19:39.761 --> 19:41.597
Nothing's really changed.

19:41.680 --> 19:44.600
We can't go out to have fun,
or hold hands!

19:44.683 --> 19:48.812
But I don't really care
since I'm a cool person!

19:48.896 --> 19:53.317
If I asked for everyone's opinion,
they'd probably say I'm a mighty woman.

19:53.400 --> 19:54.443
Could it be…

19:54.526 --> 19:56.195
It's not possible, but…

19:56.278 --> 19:59.781
It looks like Senku is ten billion percent
not interested in dating right now,

19:59.865 --> 20:02.117
and to just be saying
logical, convenient things

20:02.201 --> 20:03.827
to achieve his objective,

20:03.911 --> 20:08.749
but surely he can't be so messed up
to say such things!

20:10.792 --> 20:14.546
He even got married
to achieve his objectives.

20:14.630 --> 20:15.589
Get married?

20:15.672 --> 20:17.758
And divorced, too.

20:17.841 --> 20:19.468
Divorced?

20:27.351 --> 20:30.479
It has finally arrived!

20:34.233 --> 20:35.776
It looks like it's starting.

20:36.610 --> 20:38.820
This science showdown…

20:56.588 --> 20:58.799
I've been waiting for you, Stanley!

21:24.700 --> 21:28.495
I'll show you what
a professional flight looks like.

21:28.578 --> 21:31.873
This is to avenge Senku. The final battle!

21:33.250 --> 21:35.377
I'm still alive, though.

22:01.778 --> 22:03.947
It's science versus science…

22:05.115 --> 22:06.575
dogfight!

22:13.040 --> 22:15.959
YOU FOUND
AN AIRCRAFT CARRIER AND AN AIRPLANE

23:53.140 --> 23:55.934
NEXT EPISODE

23:56.017 --> 23:58.478
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:58.562 --> 24:00.939
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM MAY BE
DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL, SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:01.022 --> 24:01.982
Subtitle translation by: Silvia
